obs mantra-commit-v2 carries one tab-separated file row per path; tab rather than the elder space, since a tracked path may hold a space and v1's parser splits a row at the first one
obs an elder v1 blob lifts to a single entry whose path is empty, and weave_for reads that as the weave a path inherits until it has its own, so the frozen elder store answers exactly as it did
obs the control tells four things apart in pairs -- reader-loses-path from writer-drops-prior, elder dispatch from elder fallback -- because either pair read as one number would let half of it rot while green
